From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:14:25 +0000
Subject: Move settings rows to their pages

Some settings rows that this browser adds are on pages that do not match
what they do. Move them:
- "Android fonts fingerprinting mitigation" from Developer options to
  Privacy and security, because it is a privacy protection and Developer
  options stays hidden until it is unlocked.
- "Extra memory checks" from Privacy and security to Developer options,
  because it is a debugging aid, not a privacy setting.
- "Turn off pull to refresh" and "Always show toolbar" from Accessibility
  to Appearance, because they change how pages scroll and look.
- The "Text selection menu" section from Accessibility to Appearance,
  because it sets which actions the menu shows.
- The "Navigation gestures" section from Accessibility to Appearance,
  because it sets how the browser responds to gestures.

No existing preference key, feature name, default or stored value
changes. The moved switches that had no preference key get one, so that
settings search finds them on their new pages.

